  "lessons": [
    {
      "id": "cb9-l1",
      "title": "IF and ELSE",
      "xp": 15,
      "intro": [
        "IF BALANCE < 0 runs the next statements only when the condition is true. ELSE gives the other way, and END-IF closes the IF.",
        "Before END-IF existed (1985), a period ended the IF. That made bugs easy: a period too early ended the IF in the middle. Always close with END-IF.",
        "Conditions use =, <, >, <=, >= or the words EQUAL TO, LESS THAN, GREATER THAN, and NOT."
      ],
      "example": {
        "code": [
          "       IDENTIFICATION DIVISION.",
          "       PROGRAM-ID. ACCOUNT.",
          "       DATA DIVISION.",
          "       WORKING-STORAGE SECTION.",
          "       01 BALANCE  PIC S9(5)V99 VALUE -250.",
          "       PROCEDURE DIVISION.",
          "           IF BALANCE < 0",
          "               DISPLAY \"OVERDRAWN\"",
          "           ELSE",
          "               DISPLAY \"IN CREDIT\"",
          "           END-IF.",
          "           IF BALANCE IS LESS THAN -100",
          "               DISPLAY \"CALL THE CUSTOMER\"",
          "           END-IF.",
          "           STOP RUN."
        ],
        "output": [
          "OVERDRAWN",
          "CALL THE CUSTOMER"
        ]
      },
      "exercises": [
        {
