    {
      "id": "cb9-l3",
      "title": "EVALUATE",
      "xp": 15,
      "intro": [
        "When there are many choices, EVALUATE is clearer than nested IFs. EVALUATE TRUE checks one WHEN condition after another and runs the first one that's true.",
        "EVALUATE can also look at a field: EVALUATE REGION WHEN \"N\" … WHEN \"S\" …. WHEN 1 THRU 5 covers a range, and WHEN OTHER catches everything else.",
        "Several WHENs in a row share the statements after them. END-EVALUATE closes it all."
      ],
      "example": {
        "code": [
          "       IDENTIFICATION DIVISION.",
          "       PROGRAM-ID. TAX.",
          "       DATA DIVISION.",
          "       WORKING-STORAGE SECTION.",
          "       01 INCOME   PIC 9(6) VALUE 35000.",
          "       01 RATE     PIC 99.",
          "       01 DAY-NO   PIC 9 VALUE 6.",
          "       PROCEDURE DIVISION.",
          "           EVALUATE TRUE",
          "               WHEN INCOME < 10000",
          "                   MOVE 0 TO RATE",
          "               WHEN INCOME < 50000",
          "                   MOVE 20 TO RATE",
          "               WHEN OTHER",
          "                   MOVE 40 TO RATE",
          "           END-EVALUATE.",
          "           DISPLAY \"TAX RATE: \" RATE \"%\".",
          "           EVALUATE DAY-NO",
          "               WHEN 1 THRU 5",
          "                   DISPLAY \"WORKDAY\"",
          "               WHEN 6",
          "               WHEN 7",
          "                   DISPLAY \"WEEKEND\"",
          "           END-EVALUATE.",
          "           STOP RUN."
        ],
        "output": [
          "TAX RATE: 20%",
          "WEEKEND"
        ]
      },
      "exercises": [
        {
          "id": "cb9-l3-e1",
          "type": "multiple_choice",
          "prompt": "What does EVALUATE TRUE do?",
          "options": [
            "Runs the statements of the first WHEN whose condition is true",
            "Runs every WHEN",
            "Checks if TRUE is true",
            "Loops until TRUE"
          ],
          "answer": 0,
          "explanation": "Like a chain of IF … ELSE IF."
        },
